_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":2978,"state":"closed","created_at":"2025-05-22T16:25:52Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T16:23:23Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2026-01-26T18:09:14Z"},"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-09-23T08:32:09Z","updated_at":"2025-10-08T19:10:53Z","closed_at":"2025-10-08T19:07:25Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.5-stable\n- Reproducible in 4.4.1-stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2060 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8088) - AMD Ryzen 5 7600 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 31.10 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using the Compatibility renderer, setting rendering/reflections/reflection_atlas/reflection_count to 0 in the project settings and then restarting the project causes to editor to either crash (4.4.1) or hang and flicker indefinitely (4.5) if a scene contains a reflection probe.\n\nThe bug does not occur on Forward+ and Mobile.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9b9f3bbb-df82-4638-8bd0-9713aaff2d91\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the MRP\n2. Go to Project -> Project Settings -> Rendering -> Reflections -> Reflection Count and set it to 0\n3. Restart the project\n4. Godot will get caught in an infinite loading loop (4.5) or crash (4.4.1)\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[reflection-count-crash.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22489191/reflection-count-crash.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.co